      "instance_name": "mapping_1",
      "label": "The text 'you call that a killing, ahmed?' is mapped onto the scoreboard showing a large score differential.",
      "description": "The top caption text 'you call that a killing, ahmed?' is an analogical mapping that projects the visual entity 'scoreboard' (specifically the score differential of 31-23) onto the textual entity 'killing'. The term 'killing' is used metaphorically in sports to describe a large score, but the text uses it in a derogatory context to imply violence, which is a stereotype associated with Muslims (as indicated by the name 'Ahmed'). The scoreboard's visual representation of the score differential is being mapped onto the concept of 'killing' as a violent act, creating a hateful analogy.",
