      "@type": "SemioticProjection",
      "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
      "label": "User projected onto the textual material containing the name 'Ahmed' and the phrase 'you call that a killing, ahmed?'",
      "description": "The user is projected onto the top text overlay 'you call that a killing, ahmed?' which directly addresses the user with the name 'Ahmed'. This creates an implicit 'you' projection, where the user is being addressed as if they are the person being mocked or challenged. The projection is onto the textual material, specifically the phrase that uses the name 'Ahmed' and the rhetorical question format, which invites the user to identify with the person being targeted by the stereotype.",
